From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: correct the MT6797 ROM patch 1_0 digest

The first Phase A boot stopped common initialization with -EINVAL before
any WMT command. The pinned SHA-256 of ROMv3_patch_1_0_hdr.bin had its
last eight bytes mistyped, so the retained patch never matched and the
sequence refused it, as designed.

Use the file's actual digest. No step, order or check changes.

Unsigned experiment draft; archive identity is non-certifying.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c
index 356a3e6c5..37f9b41cc 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c
@@ -1421,7 +1421,7 @@ static const struct {
 	{ "mediatek/mt6797/ROMv3_patch_1_0_hdr.bin", {
 		0x45, 0x0c, 0x2b, 0x09, 0x49, 0xcf, 0x87, 0x92, 0x17, 0xac, 0x9a, 0xef,
 		0x81, 0xb1, 0x8b, 0x86, 0x09, 0x82, 0xf0, 0xe6, 0x93, 0x40, 0x78, 0x4b,
-		0x44, 0x8c, 0xf6, 0x30, 0x80, 0xb4, 0x3c, 0xf6 } },
+		0x44, 0x8b, 0x54, 0x36, 0x5d, 0x8c, 0xf6, 0x30 } },
 };
 
 static int mt6797_consys_init_rail(struct regulator *rail, bool on, bool *state)
